<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Padfire Rust - Third-Party Licenses</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 70rem; padding: 0 1rem; }
    a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .license { border-top: 1px solid currentColor; margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1rem; }
    .license-text { overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .license-used-by li { margin: .15rem 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>Padfire Rust - Third-Party Licenses</h1>
    <p>This file lists the third-party Rust crates included in Padfire Rust and reproduces the license text selected for each crate. It is generated from <code>rust/Cargo.lock</code> using <code>cargo-about</code>.</p>
    <p>Scope: the Linux x86-64 and Windows x86-64 release targets, all workspace features, and runtime, build, development, direct, and transitive dependencies. A crate may be included because it is required only on one supported target or by a build/test feature.</p>
    <p>Padfire-authored source and documentation are licensed under MIT; see the repository <code>LICENSE</code>. This notice covers third-party dependencies only. Each upstream crate remains subject to its own license and copyright notices.</p>

    <h2>License overview</h2>
    <ul>
      {{#each overview}}
      <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}} crate entries)</li>
      {{/each}}
    </ul>

    <h2>License texts and corresponding crates</h2>
    {{#each licenses}}
    <section class="license">
      <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
      <h4>Used by</h4>
      <ul class="license-used-by">
        {{#each used_by}}
        <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
        {{/each}}
      </ul>
      <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
    </section>
    {{/each}}
  </main>
</body>
</html>
